WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:02.379
Quote, the world finally knows the truth.

00:00:02.379 --> 00:00:06.230
That statement coming from writer E. Jean
Carroll after she won her civil lawsuit against

00:00:06.230 --> 00:00:07.230
Donald Trump.

00:00:07.230 --> 00:00:11.270
A federal jury in Manhattan found that trump
sexually abused Carroll in a department store

00:00:11.270 --> 00:00:15.960
dressing room in the '90s and defamed her
by denying her claim.

00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:18.200
Trump has been ordered to pay Carroll $5 million.

00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:25.509
The former president reacting on his social
media platform.

00:00:25.509 --> 00:00:33.590
&gt;&gt; What else do you expect from a trump appointed
hating judge who made sure that the result

00:00:33.590 --> 00:00:38.129
of this trial was as negative as it possibly
could be.

00:00:38.129 --> 00:00:45.000
Speaking to and in control of a jury from
an anti-Trump area which is probably the worst

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:49.380
place in the United States for me to get a
fair trial.

00:00:49.380 --> 00:00:51.559
We will be appealing this decision.

00:00:51.559 --> 00:00:52.559
It's a disgrace.

00:00:52.559 --> 00:00:53.559
[8:23:57 AM]

00:00:53.559 --> 00:00:54.559
It's a disgrace.

00:00:54.559 --> 00:00:55.680
&gt;&gt; We should note it was an anonymous jury.

00:00:55.680 --> 00:00:59.200
Joining us is E. Jean Carroll and her attorney
Roberta Kaplan.

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:00.519
Welcome.

00:01:00.519 --> 00:01:01.519
&gt;&gt; Thank you for having us.

00:01:01.519 --> 00:01:05.420
&gt;&gt; We will remember that you said I am trying
to get my life back.

00:01:05.420 --> 00:01:06.420
&gt;&gt; Yes.

00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:08.149
&gt;&gt; I am here to try to get my life back.

00:01:08.149 --> 00:01:13.030
&gt;&gt; Yes, yesterday was so -- that was such
a happy -- I was such a happy woman.

00:01:13.030 --> 00:01:15.860
I felt like we had accomplished that.

00:01:15.860 --> 00:01:16.860
&gt;&gt; You did.

00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:17.860
&gt;&gt; Yeah.

00:01:17.860 --> 00:01:24.550
&gt;&gt; Talk about what you were thinking as the
jury's decisions were read off in your mind

00:01:24.550 --> 00:01:27.630
--
&gt;&gt; We were sitting there like this.

00:01:27.630 --> 00:01:31.960
Robbie's hand, it was like holding a block
of ice.

00:01:31.960 --> 00:01:36.750
And we didn't have any idea what the jury
was going to do.

00:01:36.750 --> 00:01:38.950
The former president is incorrect.

00:01:38.950 --> 00:01:40.640
The jury was not from Manhattan.

00:01:40.640 --> 00:01:42.240
Where was it from, Robbie?

00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:44.790
&gt;&gt; Mostly westchester and north.

00:01:44.790 --> 00:01:45.790
&gt;&gt; Yeah.

00:01:45.790 --> 00:01:49.159
Six men, three women.

00:01:49.159 --> 00:01:51.260
His kind of jury, actually.

00:01:51.260 --> 00:01:54.119
And so when the verdict came in, she squeezed
my hand so hard I

00:01:54.119 --> 00:01:55.119
[8:24:59 AM]

00:01:55.119 --> 00:02:00.650
she squeezed my hand so hard I almost yelped,
but it was a great moment.

00:02:00.650 --> 00:02:07.049
&gt;&gt; What about when that first finding was
found, that this jury found that trump did

00:02:07.049 --> 00:02:09.280
not rape you?

00:02:09.280 --> 00:02:10.320
What about that moment?

00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:12.700
&gt;&gt; Robbie can explain the legal --
&gt;&gt; Sure.

00:02:12.700 --> 00:02:14.040
And I want you to.

00:02:14.040 --> 00:02:17.930
But what went through your head when you heard
that?

00:02:17.930 --> 00:02:22.739
&gt;&gt; Well, I just immediately say into my head,
oh, yes, you did, oh, yes, you did.

00:02:22.739 --> 00:02:24.590
See, that's my response.

00:02:24.590 --> 00:02:29.860
&gt;&gt; Look, New York law on sexual crimes like
this is complicated and probably not appropriate

00:02:29.860 --> 00:02:31.470
for morning viewers.

00:02:31.470 --> 00:02:36.170
The truth of the matter is, if it's sexual
abuse, which he was found guilty of, is a

00:02:36.170 --> 00:02:37.400
very, very serious offense.

00:02:37.400 --> 00:02:44.760
I am not going to get in the body parts with
you it's a very serious offense.

00:02:44.760 --> 00:02:49.820
Most importantly, she wanted her name back
as you said at the beginning.

00:02:49.820 --> 00:02:53.540
She got her name back and the jury found that
he lied and he lied about her maliciously.

00:02:53.540 --> 00:02:54.540
&gt;&gt; I don't think anybody was

00:02:54.540 --> 00:02:55.540
[8:26:00 AM]

00:02:55.540 --> 00:02:57.940
&gt;&gt; I don't think anybody was surprised by
the stuff we heard from the former president

00:02:57.940 --> 00:02:59.209
last night.

00:02:59.209 --> 00:03:01.599
You addressed him talking about the jury.

00:03:01.599 --> 00:03:06.650
Another thing he and his lawyers often spoke
about is the lack of disclosure about a big

00:03:06.650 --> 00:03:09.420
democratic donor funding part of this case.

00:03:09.420 --> 00:03:10.680
Was there a reason it wasn't disclosed?

00:03:10.680 --> 00:03:13.379
Did you view this as political in any way?

00:03:13.379 --> 00:03:14.379
&gt;&gt; No.

00:03:14.379 --> 00:03:21.090
I completely -- it was -- I just completely
forgot that he even existed.

00:03:21.090 --> 00:03:22.090
&gt;&gt; In your deposition?

00:03:22.090 --> 00:03:24.549
&gt;&gt; Yes, in my deposition.

00:03:24.549 --> 00:03:27.840
&gt;&gt; Because trump lawyers have called is that,
Roberta, a sign of bias.

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:33.450
It raises questions about the motives of bringing
this case and I wonder what the reaction is.

00:03:33.450 --> 00:03:38.250
&gt;&gt; Every single witness, every one of those
11 witnesses who testified in this case testified

00:03:38.250 --> 00:03:42.540
under oath and told the truth not because
they don't like trump, but because it was

00:03:42.540 --> 00:03:43.580
the truth.

00:03:43.580 --> 00:03:45.340
That's what this case was about.

00:03:45.340 --> 00:03:46.340
Who was telling the truth?

00:03:46.340 --> 00:03:48.750
The jury decided that E. Jean was telling
the truth.

00:03:48.750 --> 00:03:50.890
There may be witnesses who don't like trump.

00:03:50.890 --> 00:03:54.750
There may have been jurors that Joe tacopina
said don't like trump.

00:03:54.750 --> 00:03:57.569
That process was about the truth under the
law and that's what

00:03:57.569 --> 00:03:58.569
[8:27:02 AM]

00:03:58.569 --> 00:03:59.569
under the law and that's what the jury found.

00:03:59.569 --> 00:04:04.040
&gt;&gt; I don't want to make this a political conversation
but the dissonance between the moment yesterday

00:04:04.040 --> 00:04:06.290
on the front pages of all.

00:04:06.290 --> 00:04:08.670
Newspapers, getting your life back.

00:04:08.670 --> 00:04:11.780
Something you have been thinking about and
going through for decades and at the same

00:04:11.780 --> 00:04:16.060
